WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.700
1,515 frames, one Moon.

2
00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:07.600
Straight off the camera, it looked like this.

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.300
The Moon, data: 353,988 km away; 7 clips of 4K at 60 fps and 254 RAW stills; 1,400 video frames and 115 stills used.

4
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:17.400
Only the sharpest 6% of video frames made the cut.

5
00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:22.500
The Moon was too big for one frame, so I stitched five.

6
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:27.000
Then sharpening, and the Moon's real mineral color.

7
00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:31.300
Its rays, one frame against the final.

8
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:37.000
Those are real stars, where they sat that night. Composite: star positions from the Tycho-2 catalog.

9
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:41.600
Framing the Cosmos. Some things you have to stack.

